WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.612
Here's what Learn gives you:
one page with three workflows.

2
00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:06.545
One signs in and runs
a single Azure command,

3
00:00:06.545 --> 00:00:10.375
one adds PowerShell, and one
signs in to Azure Government.

4
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:13.061
Each job asks for exactly one permission,

5
00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:17.800
the right to request a sign-in token,
and keeps its identifiers in secrets.

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.116
Before any of it works,

7
00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:23.063
the app needs a federated credential
that trusts the repository.

8
00:00:23.063 --> 00:00:26.133
Those workflows only
exist inside the web page,

9
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:30.227
so the repository pins the page
and the action's own definition,

10
00:00:30.227 --> 00:00:34.400
and a linter checks each workflow
offline against twelve rules.

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.600
Nothing runs, nothing signs in.
